<title>UK: Nomura sets Japanese breakout index call warrants.</title>
<headline>Nomura sets Japanese breakout index call warrants.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nomura International said it has issued one million American-style call warrants, on an index of Tokyo listed companies.</p>
<p>The index termed 'Nomura Japanese breakout index' is based on a complex formula that includes shares of Kyocera Corp, TDK Corp, Seven Eleven, Tokyo Electron and Secom Co Ltd.</p>
<p>One warrant refers to one index.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE    5809.65 YEN	     ISSUE PRICE  $4.18</p>
<p> EXERCISE PERIOD 19.AUG.97-03.AUG.98   PAYDATE	18.AUG.97</p>
<p> LISTING	   LUXEMBOURG		SPOT REF     5533 YEN</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
